speechtext:
May I now ask the consent of the house to move the motion of which I gave notice as mentioned earlier in my remarks, in Votes and Proceedings of June 16, and which is found in the appendix opposite page 664. With the change which I mentioned in the notice when speaking on my motion for second reading, having regard to the fact that the committee now is to have referred to it only the present measure and not Bill No. C-77, an act respecting the civil service of Canada, if the house will give unanimous consent I now propose:
That a special committee be appointed to consider a bill to amend the Public Service Superannuation Act with power to send for persons, papers and records and to report from time to time;
That the committee have power to print such papers and evidence from day to day as may be deemed advisable or necessary;
That the committee shall consist of 15 members to be designated by the house;
That the committee be empowered to sit during the sittings of the house;
That standing order 66 be suspended in relation thereto.
If that motion meets with the approval of the house, I have the names of the members of the committee.
